		<bioghist encodinganalog="545">
			<head>Biographical Note</head>
			<p>William Bronk (1918-1999) was a significant 20th century American poet. His work
				garnered much acclaim, including the 1982 National Book Award.</p>
		</bioghist>
		<scopecontent encodinganalog="520">
			<head>Scope and Content Note</head>
			<p>Correspondence, manuscripts, broadsides and other material by or related to American poet William
				Bronk. Some of the correspondence is from James L. Weil, one of Bronk's
				publishers.</p>
		</scopecontent>
